ww.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T06:45:15-07:00","id":1415061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rj.au</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415044-two-questions-immaculate-order-predate-realm-islands-south-of-blessed-isle-named?p=1415049#post1415049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The largest of the three islands is Radimel's Seat. The other two aren't named.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will add that one thing we do know is that one of the islands to the west of Radimel's Seat (probably not one of the ones you're talking about from my guess of what you're counting as a BIG island) is called Shanshin - it was used by a opium smugglers who have since relocated to Arjuf (Realm, p29 if you have it to hand).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T10:56:23-07:00","id":1415087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415044-two-questions-immaculate-order-predate-realm-islands-south-of-blessed-isle-named#post1415044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we know whether the Immaculate Order predates the Realm? I seem to remember that a version of the Immaculate Order also exists in Lookshy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, there's the Immaculate Philosophy; that's the system of belief that says the Elemental Dragons created the world and it is sustained through the Perfected Hierarchy whereby all things gradually rise up to join the perfected state of the Dragons, with the Exalted as those at the top, and the mythology of the Immaculate Dragons who liberated the world from the Anathema.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Order is the hierarchical organisation of monks that promotes and administers the Philosophy in the Realm, and is intertwined with its institutions.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Faith is the term for the practice of the Philosophy in Lookshy. They still have monks as dedicated spiritual guides, but they're a lot less rigidly organised and basically have no function in Lookshy's government. They also deviate in how much authority they invest in the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Philosophy began in the Shogunate, and it did have an Immaculate Order organised around it then. We're never told very much about the practice during that period, but I infer that there was enough of an Order for Chejop to harness them towards supporting the Scarlet Empress. The Immaculate Faith in Lookshy implies to me variations in how people thought the Philosophy ought to function, so I presume that whatever Order it had was not quite so powerful as they are in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Still, per Third Edition, the Philosophy was still big enough to have a lot of rich shrines and similar holy sites in the city of Juche in the heart of the Blessed Isle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}